  {
   "key": "0x110",
   "name": "reset ext/status ints",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
     "lines": "6428-6444"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "function": "z80scc_channel::do_sccreg_wr0",
     "case": [
      "WR0_RESET_EXT_STATUS"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "WR0 command code 010 is the Reset External/Status Interrupts command: after an External/Status interrupt it re-enables the latched RR0 status bits so a change can interrupt again.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6428-6434",
       "sha": "7565fa51f7a217de356035a5a5ee63834378a88b2da56788aa522f7523cb3c8f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Latching the status bits captures short pulses until the CPU has time to read the change.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6433-6434",
       "sha": "428998598bec66e7a1d90de3a2bdbd4f173cba782cb34b4c0d2c8dc6e4e9adcb"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "If another condition changes while one is pending and persists past the command, it causes another interrupt; two transitions do not.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6435-6444",
       "sha": "1adca68525332ae2b0369e8005d6adc906dcf2bef4546f228e81200da54787f2"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
