  {
   "key": "0x118",
   "name": "send abort",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
     "lines": "6445-6448"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "function": "z80scc_channel::do_sccreg_wr0",
     "case": [
      "WR0_SEND_ABORT"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Send Abort is command code 011.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6445",
       "sha": "3d51afd3b7ec39a81451c1dce3190d97c27ef311aa9bc57a14800a2d064b4063"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Send Abort, in SDLC mode (printed SOLC in the scan), transmits eight to thirteen 1s and empties the transmit buffer, setting the Tx Underrun/EOM bit in RR0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6445-6448",
       "sha": "1544820cd10adf1f644e6e807a19124d1644340eb7484cb6768fcaa88fbcde5d"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "absent",
     "text": "MAME logs the command as not implemented: the case body sends nothing, empties no transmit buffer and touches no Tx Underrun/EOM bit.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
       "lines": "1813-1815",
       "sha": "0962b45f638e40edb7bc0c2505a66dc93f357749d64607bfdb0493959d3cb934"
      }
     ],
     "row": "2"
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "lines": "1746",
     "as": "structure"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "key": "0x120",
   "name": "enable int on next Rx",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
     "lines": "6449-6455"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "function": "z80scc_channel::do_sccreg_wr0",
     "case": [
      "WR0_ENABLE_INT_NEXT_RX"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "function": "z80scc_channel::check_receive_interrupt"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Enable Interrupt on Next Rx Character is command code 100.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6449",
       "sha": "3eafcebb1300e4d7663f604a347214a2b85f411c8a8007121defdd5b9b91c11e"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "If Interrupt on First Received Character mode is selected, the command reactivates it, so the next character, or one already stored, causes a Receive interrupt.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6449-6455",
       "sha": "2af829dc722e8b5c98c04538d7129fc089ac9d2341896dd610138a885fe021ca"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "2",
     "text": "MAME arms the interrupt for the next character received; a character already in the FIFO raises none, as nothing checks the flag when the command is written.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
       "lines": "1819-1822",
       "sha": "0a20fede2d5b115e4d01511dcbbbd11c51feaa41bab67e157eae22f8dbe8edf8"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
       "lines": "3033-3042",
       "sha": "56738951daa28ead72c94d2fb88fc44fa46d89cf294effddb9efdeadabda05fd"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
