  {
   "key": "0x128",
   "name": "reset Tx int pending",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
     "lines": "6456-6464"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "function": "z80scc_channel::do_sccreg_wr0",
     "case": [
      "WR0_RESET_TX_INT"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "lines": "1250"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "lines": "1265"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Reset Tx Interrupt Pending is command code 101, used when there are no more characters to send, for example at the end of a message.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6456-6458",
       "sha": "c674f2174768e099d9eec3e961d5e2d105f597a2b7c8c1fa5c0fc3c54477f479"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "It prevents further transmit interrupts until the next character is loaded or CRC has been sent, with transmit interrupt enabled.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6458-6464",
       "sha": "3077f5f82ac57cd36b37e5d9cc4a70f950a89b2c7ec3ea3f43b72c1c32fd4713"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "MAME also clears the channel's transmit entry in the interrupt state and its bit in RR3, then re-evaluates the interrupt line.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
       "lines": "1831-1835",
       "sha": "98fa8a181eed3cd76462a3be98adf74f1245e3c729d672fd6947b17368ec03e1"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
