  {
   "key": "0x130",
   "name": "error reset",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
     "lines": "6465-6472"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "function": "z80scc_channel::do_sccreg_wr0",
     "case": [
      "WR0_ERROR_RESET"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "lines": "2387-2398"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Error Reset is command code 110.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6465",
       "sha": "97f0ed2191a2e3a0ec5165a2c7cdbe67e0e47ab35f0376e4f27bf510ad884ced"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The command resets the error bits in RR1.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6465-6466",
       "sha": "b5f1e826b08589fa7a7f449a41d8be1ed80628bacd61e022e9faf80711e29783"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "With interrupt on first Rx character or on special condition selected, data with a special condition waits until this command, which loses it if issued before the read.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6466-6472",
       "sha": "0ef21102978ac0458f89ab2e430f79e880a11b651f69060cca9781e2ce8b7436"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "differs",
     "text": "MAME does not reset the RR1 error bits: with a character in the FIFO it steps the read pointer, dropping that character, and otherwise it only logs.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
       "lines": "1809-1811",
       "sha": "22fe4000f253592f1dac736a22edb124f0d621502350007d7fc61934d0816bd1"
      }
     ],
     "row": "2"
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
    {
