  {
   "key": "0x138",
   "name": "reset highest IUS",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
     "lines": "6473-6478"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "function": "z80scc_channel::do_sccreg_wr0",
     "case": [
      "WR0_RESET_HIGHEST_IUS"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The capture names this command Reset Highest IUS and prints its code as (110); the key of this entry is 111.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6473",
       "sha": "7e181a2f1946443dd7d16491fb9789c907839f3f452c4b9bf953e2b8f5839657"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The command resets the highest priority Interrupt Under Service bit, allowing lower priority conditions to request interrupts.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6473-6475",
       "sha": "be164c563532b3b36afebd4a18f248ea5069f2adf4499ad4e8a84e30ede32baa"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "It allows the internal daisy chain to be used even without an external one, and is the last operation in an interrupt service routine.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SCC-UserManual-1992.raw.txt",
       "lines": "6475-6478",
       "sha": "2d4912444d5a8e2f8684728c761944678778017b59066b0a56040505f6012d0d"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "MAME zeroes the whole interrupt-state entry of that source, dropping its pending request with the in-service bit.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
       "lines": "1795",
       "sha": "02260f2b4601d2ed562f70efcb0b7570acfecfbae533344992e4e1829c725179"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "After clearing the bit MAME re-checks the receive interrupt condition.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
       "lines": "1800-1801",
       "sha": "ce46e436177d57fd4397d957f6c364df72cfe648d171966b4e136126f3c6b59a"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "lines": "1746",
     "as": "structure"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80scc.cpp",
     "lines": "1789-1797",
     "as": "agrees",
     "row": "2"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "key": "0x200..0x23F",
   "name": "WR9 no reset",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
